## Why This Is Asked

Stresses runtime extensibility and safety: add formats without redeploying core, using a registry to decouple format handling from ingestion logic.

## Key Concepts

- Plugin architecture
- Runtime registry
- Strategy for Parse/Validate contracts
- Versioned schemas and migration
- Fault tolerance and fallback

## Code Example

```typescript
// Minimal interfaces and usage
interface Parser { parse(input: any): NormalizedRecord }
interface Validator { validate(rec: NormalizedRecord): boolean }
interface NormalizedRecord { id: string; payload: any }
class Registry { registerParser(fmt: string, p: Parser); getParser(fmt: string): Parser | null }
class Orchestrator { constructor(private reg: Registry, private val: Validator) {}
  ingest(input: any, fmt: string){ const p = reg.getParser(fmt); if(!p) throw new Error('No parser');
  const rec = p.parse(input); if(!val.validate(rec)) throw new Error('Invalid');
  sink(rec); } }
```

